+## Customer experience 
+
+#### 1. Select payment method
+
+The customer selects Przelewy24 at checkout.
+
+#### 2. Choose bank
+
+The customer is redirected to Przelewy24 and chooses a bank.
+
+#### 3. Enter credentials
+
+The customer enters their account credentials.
+
+#### 4. Authorize payment
+
+The customer completes the authorization process within one hour of checkout.
+
+#### 5. Payment complete
+
+The customer is notified that payment is complete.
+
+#### 6. Return to site
+
+The customer returns to the business's site for payment confirmation.
+
+### Transaction Identifiers 
+
+After a customer completes a P24 payment, the transaction appears on their bank statement. The statement entry includes a unique P24 reference number followed by your statement descriptor, in the format:
+
+```
+/OPT/X/////P24-XXX-XXX-XXX {your statement descriptor}
+```
+
+Set a custom [statement descriptor](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/payment-intents.md#dynamic-statement-descriptor) on the PaymentIntent before confirming the payment. If you don’t set one, the descriptor defaults to the [account level statement descriptor](https://docs.stripe.com/get-started/account/statement-descriptors.md). For connect scenarios, learn more on how [statement descriptors are set with Connect](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/statement-descriptors.md).
+
+After the payment completes, expand `latest_charge` on the PaymentIntent to retrieve the P24 reference number from `latest_charge.payment_method_details.p24.reference`. Share it with customers to help them locate the payment on their bank statement.
+
+## Enable P24 
+
+If you use our front-end products, you can enable P24 directly from your [payment method settings](https://dashboard.stripe.com/settings/payment_methods). Stripe then automatically determines the most relevant payment methods to display to your customers.
+
+If your integration requires manually listing payment methods, learn how to [manually configure P24 as a payment](https://docs.stripe.com/payments/p24/accept-a-payment.md).
+
+For connected accounts that use the Express Dashboard or no Stripe-hosted Dashboard, follow the instructions to [request capabilities for your connected accounts](https://docs.stripe.com/connect/account-capabilities.md#requesting-unrequesting). Request the `p24_payments` capability and check that its status is `active` before accepting P24 payments.